Description: StreamIO: read HTTP/ICY through the network kit's request
 The stream adapter (BAdapterIO) built on the legacy byte-stream
 interface has no counterpart on V\OS, so StreamIO becomes its own sink
 and buffer: the network kit's BHttpRequest writes the response body
 into it (BDataIO::Write), the ICY metadata blocks are stripped by the
 upstream DataFunc chain unchanged, and the audio bytes land in a
 bounded ring buffer whose Read() applies backpressure to the request
 thread. Headers, redirects, icy-metaint handling and the meta message
 are the upstream logic; strlwr (a helper V\OS does not ship) becomes a
 local lowercase loop. AdapterIO.h and AdapterIO.cpp are deleted: they
 implement the legacy byte-stream interface V\OS does not ship.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: vendor
Last-Update: 2026-10-21
